{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/331461-what-happens-when-a-shadow-resolves-a-dark-passion","id":331461,"title":"What happens when a *Shadow* Resolves a *Dark Passion*?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-05T14:03:28-08:00","id":331461,"title":"What happens when a *Shadow* Resolves a *Dark Passion*?","content":"Greetings all,<br /> <br /> I've asked this question a number of times in a bunch of different places, but have only received a couple of responses - so in the hopes of generating more ideas (and perhaps an official-ish answer from Deadguy himself - because this *might* be something worth having in Wr20's Shadow section *poke-poke*) I'm cut 'n' pasting this here one last time; Thanks in advance:<br /> <br /> <br /> &gt;&gt;<br /> Once upon a time, during a game I was running, we had a player whose character was framed for a murder he didn't commit, whose Shadow had the Dark Passion &quot;Kill the 'Twelve Good Men' (Revenge) &quot; who sent him to the electric chair. During the course of the game (before it ended due to real life pressures), the Shadow had managed to arrange the death of at least *3* members of said Jury. It was only at this point that we had realised that there were no rules or guidelines in the game on what happens when a Shadow *succeeds* in Resolving a Dark Passion.<br /> My players and I (and a few posters from the ye olde Wraith List) came up with a few possible solutions (eg. All Dark Passion dots immediately convert to Permanent Angst; Dark Passion dots are converted to Thorn points/ Shadow Xp/ divided up amongst the remaining Dark Passions; The Dark Passion's Focus expands or widens [eg. the family members and work mates of the jury members now become the targets of the Shadow's Revenge].<br /> Because the game ended, we never ended up deciding on an actual house rule on what to do *if* the Dark Passion ever got Resolved...so, I was just wondering if anyone ever encountered a similar situation in their games (and how they chose to deal with it), or just what anyone thinks *should* happen, in their opinion.<br /> &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is the Line of Division...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3797-terminus-est","name":"Terminus Est","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3797_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T21:28:00-08:00","id":331894,"title":"","content":"You know, that's an excellent question...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T09:37:47-08:00","id":332248,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't is be interesting if resolving a Dark Passion worked towards moving the wraith towards Transcendence, just like a non-Dark Passion? Sure the Shadow is compelled to do this, but, it's still resolving something that was dragging down the wraith, just something that was dragging down his darker urges made manifest. So, the resolution actually lifts the total &quot;karmic weight.&quot; I dunno. Have to think about it some.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T10:17:59-08:00","id":332268,"title":"","content":"Resolving a Passion is a huge moment, so resolving a Dark Passion should be equally huge for the Shadow.<br /> The thing is, Dark Passions almost always target things that are important to the wraith negatively. Whether it is destroying a Fetter, perverting a Passion or in some other way twisting something the wraith holds dear, the ultimate goal of a Dark Passion is to remove every connection the wraith has to the world of the living and drag it into Oblivion.<br /> <br /> In a way, the Shadow struggles with the Psyche over a sort of antitranscendence, the descent into Oblivion. If the Psyche wins, the wraith resolves it's Passions peacefully and embraces Transcendence. If the Shadow wins, the wraith is consumed by Oblivion. Two sides of the same coin.<br /> <br /> The process of resolving a Dark Passion should reflect this, though I don't have any good ideas about what should happen.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the Shadow merely gains permanent Angst, or maybe the internal struggle weakens the wraiths grip on it's psyche and the wraith loses a point of permanent Corpus. Perhaps the wraith is even thrown immediately into a destruction harrowing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4449-eisenkreutzer","name":"EisenKreutzer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4449_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T18:32:44-08:00","id":333647,"title":"","content":"Personally I think that the Shadow is incapable of &quot;resolving&quot; a Dark Passion; if they manage to succeed on the Dark Passion's goal then it will simply shift focus and likely grow. The Shadow is defined as selfishness personified, and selfishness doesn't end when it's demands are met; I would say that makes them worse.<br /> <br /> The psyche can hope to resolve dark passions as well as regular passions in my game, but resolving Dark Passions is a lot harder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T20:00:07-08:00","id":333691,"title":"","content":"I always belived that once the Shadow completes his Dark Passions, the Wraith is fully consumed on a self destructive path and becomes an Spectre of some sorts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T08:45:06-08:00","id":334230,"title":"","content":"That would encourage players to choose dark passions that are 'never' getting resolved, wouldn't it? There are some examples given in the rules that are continuous Dark Passions, that don't have a clear conclusion point/condition. ('Destroy the Hierarchy', 'Murder Firemen families with Arson', etc... its not infinite but not easy to achieve either...)<br /> Im not 100% sure on tabletop mechanics, because I'm mostly a LARP ST, but here are peeks from Oblivion (wraith official Minds Eye Theatre adaptation)<br /> <br /> * <i>The Shadow acquires Angst in several ways, including feeding its Dark Passions[...]<br /> <br /> The Shadow\u2019s goals and drives are embodied in Dark Passions, which are usually the opposite or corrupted, self-destructive versions of the Psyche\u2019s normal Passions. For example, if you had a Passion such as 'Avenge my murder' (Anger), your Shadow\u2019s Dark Passion might be 'Get revenge on anyone who disagrees with me' (Hate). There is a fine line between anger and hate, but if your character ever seeks excessive vengeance on another wraith, that might be enough for a test to see if your Shadow gains Temporary Angst.<br /> <br /> Dark Passions \u2013 If a Shadow is able to manipulate the Psyche or other wraiths into expressing one of its Dark Passions, it can call for a Simple Test. If the Shadow wins, a point of Temporary Angst is acquired. A tie indicates a retest until one side or the other actually wins. This method is only pertinent if the Shadow is actually being guided. Otherwise, Angst can only be gained from Dark Passions during Catharsis. This is done in the same manner, in which a wraith gains Pathos from her regular Passions.<br /> <br /> Dark Passions, unlike Passions, do not fade if ignored. Dark Passions can never be Numbed, and cannot be removed by any means.</i> *<br /> <br /> <br /> Just like there are Passions that are 'Resolvable' and Passions that are 'Continuous', I'm not clear on the need of a reward for resolving either.<br /> Besides, resolving Fetters sets the wraith free doesn't it? It seems to me having a clearer suggested mechanic for numbing down Passions and perhaps 'awakening' them back up would be nice, but following the suggestion that Dark Passions WILL stick around, perhaps broadening it's target/goal would be good and enough?<br /> <br /> I'm not sure on the intricacies of levels of intensities on passions, because the MET mechanics tossed that out (I dont feel it is crippled by it, if anything, removes bookkepping and allow free-er roleplayin), so bear in mind I am not considering any TableTop mechanics that might render my opinion... out of place.<br /> <br /> Hope that further insights/ideas/discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4474-ivarov","name":"Ivarov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4474_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T20:19:45-08:00","id":334781,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think if your Dark Passion is something like &quot;Get them to play better music at the nightclub&quot; then if they do, lo and behold, start to play better music then your Passion would evolve to be, &quot;Make them play better music at Every Club&quot;, or even &quot;Make them play only my music at the club.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T20:59:13-08:00","id":334796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/331461-what-happens-when-a-shadow-resolves-a-dark-passion?p=334781#post334781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I think if your Dark Passion is something like &quot;Get them to play better music at the nightclub&quot; then if they do, lo and behold, start to play better music then your Passion would evolve to be, &quot;Make them play better music at Every Club&quot;, or even &quot;Make them play only my music at the club.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats a very mild and timid Shadow you have there. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4449-eisenkreutzer","name":"EisenKreutzer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4449_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T16:54:22-08:00","id":335580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EisenKreutzer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/331461-what-happens-when-a-shadow-resolves-a-dark-passion?p=334796#post334796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a very mild and timid Shadow you have there. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an NPC's Dark Passion in the Haunts sourcebook. It was used as a springboard for discussion about the nature of the Shadow in the Shadow Player's Guide due to the character's Passions being &quot;more evil&quot; than their supposed Dark Passions.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}